                <pb facs="0547" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg381"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.00/1194</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-09T02:00:00-05:29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1917, 2 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Suggest that naval commander at Santiago have substance of President Menocal’s
                    proclamation of today posted in streets, then land battalion marines, and notify
                    rebel commander he must submit to Government or go outside city to fight federal
                    troops. This would relieve apprehension of bloodshed in city and there would
                    probably be little outside.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
